    assert.strictEqual(bytes('oops 10 MB'), null);
  });
});
"}, "note": "Removing the ^ anchor lets parseRegExp match a valid size suffix anywhere in the string, so inputs with leading garbage like 'abc1kb' now parse to 1024 instead of returning null as in 3.1.2. The unanchored regex also changes the parseInt-fallback path for inputs like ' 1kb' (previously 1, now 1024)."}
